1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Karl_Matthias_von_Lepel Wikipedia Karl Matthias von Lepel (De)]
2 CONT
2 CONT Karl Matthias von Lepel (born December 24 †, 1704) was a Prussian major.
2 CONT
2 CONT Karl Matthias was a member of the Pomeranian noble family of Lepel. His parents were the Pomeranian district councillor and heir to Netzelkow and Lütow Caspar Mathias von Lepel (1660-1723) and Eleonore Agnes von Klinckowström from
2 CONC  engelswarth (1680-1720).
2 CONT
2 CONT Lepel participated in the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Second_Silesian_War 2nd Silesian War] in 1744 as wing adjutant and commander of a Grenadierbattalion,which was composed of two companies of regiments No. 7 and No. 30 and 17
2 CONC 44 to 1745 respectively "Jung-Bornstedt" and "Alt-Woldeck".  In 1746 he was awarded the Order of Pour le Mérite. He received his farewell in 1747.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was lord of Netzelkow from his father's inheritance and, since 1727, also owned by Görmitz. In 1744 he also acquired the outstanding shares in the estate Neuendorf and Lütow from brother Carl Albrecht. All the estates on the Gn
2 CONC itz were sold together in 1753 in the family, in this case Joachim Friedrich (1712-1784).
2 CONT
2 CONT In the last year of his life, he was under administrative custody because of mental confusion (Kuratel).
2 CONT
2 CONT Lepel married Sophie Dorothea von Kleist (1728-1811) in 1747 (divorced before 1754). He had a second marriage to Eva Sophie von Ramin. From his first marriage came the son Johann Friedrich von Lepel, who had also fought an officer
2 CONC 's career in the Prussian army.
