1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT =Sir Audley Charles Gosling, KCMG=
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Audley_Charles_Gosling '''Sir Audley Charles Gosling'''], [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Order_of_St_Michael_and_St_George KCMG], was a British diplomat who served as British Minister to Chile 1897-1
2 CONC 901.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Early life and background===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gosling was born''' in 1836, the younger son of Captain Gosling, Royal Navy. He served with the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Royal_Welch_Fusiliers Royal Welsh Fusiliers] 1855-1857.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Diplomatic career===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gosling entered''' the diplomatic service in 1859, and served as Secretary of Legation in Copenhagen from 1881, and in Madrid from 1885. After a spell as Secretary of Embassy in St Petersburg 1888-1890, he was posted to Latin A
2 CONC merica for the rest of his diplomatic career. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He was appointed''' British Minister Resident to the Central American Republics in 1890, and was resident in Guatemala, also covering Honduras and El Salvador. In 1897, he was appointed Minister Resident and Consul-General to t
2 CONC he Republic of Chile, and the position was upgraded to [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Envoy_(title%29 Envoy Extraordinary and Minister Plenipotentiary] in 1899. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He resigned in late''' 1901, was appointed a [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Order_of_St_Michael_and_St_George Knight Commander of the Order of St Michael and St George] (KCMG) in the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1901_Birthday
2 CONC _Honours 1901 Birthday Honours list], and invested as such by [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edward_VII '''King Edward VII'''] at [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marlborough_House Marlborough House] on 28 December 1901.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gosling married first''', in 1858, [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Gyldenstolpe_nr_35#TAB_6 '''Ida Gyldenstolpe'''], daughter of Count August Gyldenstolpe, Chamberlain to the King of Sweden. She died in 1900, leaving five
2 CONC  children, three sons and two daughters. He married secondly, in 1904, [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/H%C3%A4gerflycht_nr_873#TAB_8 '''Augusta''', Countess '''Posse''' (née '''Hägerflycht''')], widow of Count [https://en.wi
2 CONC kipedia.org/wiki/Arvid_Posse '''Arvid Posse'''], a former Prime Minister of Sweden.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Audley Charles Gosling''' died at Southsea on 7 December 1913.
2 CONT
2 CONT /////
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Storbritanniens minister''' 1:e honorable '''Sir Audley Charles Gosling''' född 1836-11-20, † 1913-12 i England.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gift 1:o''' 1858-10-12 i Stockholm med [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Gyldenstolpe_nr_35#TAB_6 '''Augusta Sofia Vilhelmina Ida Gyldenstolpe'''] född 1837-10-20 i Stockholm, † 1900-08-25 i Marstrand.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gift 2:o''' 1904-02-29 i Cannes med [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/H%C3%A4gerflycht_nr_873#TAB_8 '''Ebba ''Augusta'' Hägerflycht'''] född 1843-08-25 på Fredriksdal, död 1911-07-15 i Stockholm Taxinge förs., Söd. 
