2 CONT
2 CONT "GOSLING, Cecil William Gustaf (1870-1944) Minister, Bolivia, 1910-16. Consul-General, Gothenburg, 1916-18; Frankfurt-am-Main, 1919-24. Charge d'Affaires, Czechoslovakia, 1918. Madame Teresa Preyre, 5 rue de Russie, Tangier, Moroc
2 CONC co, has a few speeches, addresses and reports relating to her father's career. The papers include notes on the Amazon, a copy of Gosling's long official report from La Paz (22 Dec. 1913), and speeches made in Germany and Czechoslo
2 CONC vakia. Copies of the papers are held at B.L.P.E.S. (British Library of Political and Economic Science).""
2 CONT
2 CONT C. Cook, P. Jones, J. Sinclair, Jeffrey Weeks. Sources in British Political History, 1900-1951: Volume 2: A Guide to the Private Papers of Selected Public Services. Springer, 30 Dec 2015 - Political Science - 297 pages.
